// Conversation lines (DEC-093): a reply is an opener (by the relationship),
// sometimes a memory quote, the substance (by the facts and what the speaker
// will tell) and sometimes a closer (in the speaker's voice). Every `when`
// condition must hold (the shared situation conditions; slots `speaker`,
// `about`, `player`); each adds Fluent arguments, and every line has
// `$speaker`, `$player`, `$town` and `$here` (and `$about` on topics with a
// subject). Arguments named `x_key` are Fluent keys, written `{ $x }`.
// A `remembers` condition gives `$subject` and `$subject_kind` (`bill`,
// `decision` or `none`): a quote has a variant for each, so a memory about
// nothing in particular never reads "over that business".
// `teaches` is capped at what the speaker will tell, and needs a `tells`
// condition at that level or higher. `fallback` lines are a topic's safe
// answer for the roles in their `occupation` condition (none: every role).
//
// The base set (task C3). How it is built:
// - Relationship bands, as the discretion bands: cool below −15 (hostile
//   below −50), neutral −15..15, warm from 15, trusted from 50 with trust
//   0.5. Cool speakers tell nothing, so their answers are the fallbacks,
//   which carry the role's voice (weight 3 against the shared ones' 1).
// - Openers in a voice name it (`{ "type": "voice", "voices": [...] }`),
//   so they follow the speaker's chosen voice (`voices.jsonc`): a cautious
//   charmer is smooth, opener and closer alike, never guarded then smooth.
// - Places without a proper name are named by their kind in `$here`,
//   `$about` and `$broker_place` ("the union hall", `talk-place-<kind>`).
// - `concern` conditions give `$concern` (the name, a capitalised label) and
//   `$concern_talk` (a lower-case noun phrase for mid-sentence use).
// - Substance lines say only what their conditions make true: lay-offs need
//   job losses, the clean-up a recent disaster, and so on. Expertise lines
//   (DEC-095) are a role on the facts it sees at work: a nurse on the
//   waiting room, a teacher on the register, a steward on the notices.
// - Role groups: politicians (councillor, mayor), the party (party chair),
//   workers (union steward, organiser), business (business association
//   chair, plant manager), trade (shopkeeper, diner owner), the farm, the
//   press (journalist, editor), clergy, care (teacher, nurse) and folk
//   (resident, retiree).
// Some base-file tests (`mandate-content` conversation tests) edit lines
// here by their exact text; keep the lines they name as they are.
{
  "kind": "talk_lines",
  "items": [
    // --- Openers, by relationship (any topic) -------------------------------------
    { "id": "line.open.cool", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-cool",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "max": -15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.cool.2", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-cool-2",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "max": -15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.cool.3", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-cool-3",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -50, "max": -15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.cool.4", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-cool-4",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -50, "max": -15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.hostile", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-hostile", "weight": 2,
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "max": -50 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.hostile.2", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-hostile-2", "weight": 2,
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "max": -50 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.neutral", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-neutral",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -15, "max": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.neutral.2", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-neutral-2",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -15, "max": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.neutral.3", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-neutral-3",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -15, "max": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.neutral.4", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-neutral-4",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": -15, "max": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.warm", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-warm",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.warm.2", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-warm-2",
      "when": [ { "type": "opinion", "slot": "speaker", "min": 15 } ] },
    { "id": "line.open.warm.3", "part": "opener", "key": "talk-open-warm-3",
